  "body": "I understand that the [current spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interactive-elements.html#the-dialog-element:event-cancel) is vague because we want to provide the flexibility, however it might good if we can specify more details for using escape key as the mechanism. \r\n\r\nFor example, should the cancel event get fired after the `keyup` or the `keydown` event? And if we do a preventDefault on the key event, should it prevent the dialog from being closed? \r\n\r\nThe current behaviour in Chromium is `document keydown -> window keydown -> cancel -> close -> document keyup -> window keyup`. And adding `preventDefault()` on keydown event does prevent the dialog from being closed. \r\n\r\ncc @domenic @smaug---- ",
